"epic card" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-card&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-card&gt; element: one epic's card on the Epics page, its state, link, saga, star and last-worked day.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph><text code>&lt;epic-card&gt;</> is one epic's card on the Epics page, drawn from what the epic's page says.</>
	<list bulleted>
		<item>Its state's mark before its title, by the one rule every list and page uses: in progress, errors, paused, future, done.</>
		<item>Its description, its saga's label and its meta line.</>
		<item>A star near its top right: a click stars or unstars the epic on the page server.</>
		<item>A <text code>...</> menu in its top right corner: Resume (its session in its own VS Code window), Rename Epic..., Complete and Delete Epic..., each asking first in a dialog.</>
		<item>The day it was last worked on at its bottom right, the full date its tooltip.</>
	</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone changing the Epics page's cards.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P3), in the <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/" code>epic-list</></> family, with <text code>&lt;epic-list&gt;</>, <text code>&lt;epic-card&gt;</> and <text code>&lt;epic-sort&gt;</>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list-epiccard-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicCard.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicCard.en.ts" code>EpicCard.en.ts</></></>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-list-epiccard-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicCard.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-list/EpicCard.tsx" code>EpicCard.tsx</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<example "Example">
			<html>
				<ui-stack style="max-width: 360px">
					<epic-card id="epic-epic-engine" epic="epic-engine" updated="2026-10-19" phases="done done active todo" active="P3 · Pages as Components" running worked="2026-10-19T16:13-04:00" saga="epics" saga-title="Epic Tooling" saga-purpose="Epics:  their pages, the review loop, comments, agents.">
						<a href="/epics/epic-engine/epic-engine.plan.html" target="epic-engine">Epic Engine</a>
						<span slot="description">One engine for every repo's epics.</span>
						<span slot="meta">P3 · Pages as Components · epics/epic-engine/epic-engine.plan.html</span>
					</epic-card>
				</ui-stack>
			</html>
		</example>
		<text paragraph>A running epic, mid-way: in progress, its phases done of all in a blue label. Opened without the page server's write token, its star is disabled and says why.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>A card, written as from this page:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-card
			  id="epic-airplane"
			  epic="airplane"
			  data-status="open"
			  phases="done active todo"
			  updated="2026-10-08"
			  urgent="q3"
			  active="P2 · Site Map"
			  worked="2026-10-09T14:34-04:00"
			  saga="epics"
			  saga-title="Epic Tooling"
			  saga-purpose="Epics:  their pages, the review loop ..."
			  favorite
			>
			  <a href="../../epics/airplane/airplane.plan.html" target="airplane">Airplane</a>
			  <span slot="description">Work with no Claude, on a plane.</span>
			  <span slot="meta">P2 · Site Map · epics/airplane/airplane.plan.html</span>
			</epic-card>
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Written by <link target="src-spell-epic-src-list-epiccards-ts" link="/epic/src/list/EpicCards.ts"><text title="epic/src/list/EpicCards.ts" code>epicCardHtml()</></>, for <text code>epic pages index</> and the page server alike.</>
			<item><text code>data-status</>: <text code>done</> or <text code>open</>, for the docs runtime's count and state chips.</>
			<item>The page server marks each card <text code>running</> and <text code>favorite</> as they are now, as it serves the page.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="compass"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Parent</>
				<cell>How many</>
				<cell>As</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<link target="src-spell-epic-src-docs-epic-list-html" link="/epic-list">
						<text code>&lt;epic-list&gt;</>
					</>
				</>
				<cell>any number</>
				<cell>One epic.</>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>Its children: the title link, then <text code>slot="description"</> and <text code>slot="meta"</>.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Attribute</>
				<cell>Value</>
				<cell>What it is</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell><text code>epic</> (required)</>
				<cell>an epic's name</>
				<cell>Its folder in <link target="src-epics" link="/epics/"><text code>epics/</></>: <text code>airplane</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>phases</>
				</>
				<cell>statuses, space-separated</>
				<cell>Each phase's status, in order: <text code>done done active todo</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>updated</>
				</>
				<cell>a date</>
				<cell>Its page's <text code>updated</> day: paused after 3 days without one.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>urgent</>
				</>
				<cell>item ids</>
				<cell>Its items that need you: <text code>q3 j12</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>future</>
				</>
				<cell>present or not</>
				<cell>Written down with <text code>/epic future</>, not planned yet.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>standing</>
				</>
				<cell>present or not</>
				<cell>Open for good: every phase done is not done.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>running</>
				</>
				<cell>present or not</>
				<cell>A session runs for it: never paused. The page server's to set.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>active</>
				</>
				<cell>text</>
				<cell>The phase under way: <text code>P8 · Review Polish</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>worked</>
				</>
				<cell>a time</>
				<cell>When it was last worked on: drawn as <text code>10/9</>.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell><text code>saga</>, <text code>saga-title</>, <text code>saga-purpose</></>
				<cell>a saga id, text</>
				<cell>The saga it serves: its label's words and tooltip.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>favorite</>
				</>
				<cell>present or not</>
				<cell>Starred: under Favorites, and only there.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>away</>
				</>
				<cell>present or not</>
				<cell>Its epic page has "0. While you were out" to read: a red mark under its title links it (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P62).</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>Pieces of what it draws, which a page's CSS can style from outside with <text code>::part(name)</>.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Part</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The card, a <text code>&lt;ui-card&gt;</>.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>mark</>
					</>
					<cell>Its state's mark before the title.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>saga</>
					</>
					<cell>Its saga's label, a <text code>&lt;ui-label&gt;</>.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>star</>
					</>
					<cell>The star, left of its menu, a <text code>&lt;ui-button&gt;</>.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>menu</>
					</>
					<cell>The <text code>...</> menu at its top right, a <text code>&lt;ui-dropdown&gt;</>: Resume, Rename Epic..., Complete, Delete Epic...</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>worked</>
					</>
					<cell>The day it was last worked on, a <text code>&lt;time&gt;</>.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>

		<section label="Events" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>What it tells the page.</>
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Event</>
					<cell>Detail</>
					<cell>When</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>epic-starred</>
					</>
					<cell>
						<text code>&#123; epic, favorite, favorites &#125;</>
					</>
					<cell>The page server starred or unstarred it: <text code>favorites</> is every starred epic, which its list stars every card by.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>A Spell UI card (<text code>&lt;ui-card&gt;</>), as dense as the docs pages' card grids.</>
			<item>The mark: in progress, its phases done of all (<text code>3/6</>, or <text code>planning</>) in a small blue outlined label; the rest, the state's icon in its colour.</>
			<item>The star: grey until pointed at, the page's yellow once starred (2026-10-10: "make it yellow").</>
			<item>The meta line in the brand's mono, small.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>epic pages index</>, from each epic page; the page server, for an epic still in its worktree.</>
			<item>Its menu asks the page server (<text code>/api/epics/manage</>, <text code>EpicLifecycle</>): what it would refuse first (a worktree, a branch not merged, the tooling home), then the change. Resume runs <text code>epic window launch &lt;name&gt; --prompt "/epic resume &lt;name&gt;"</>; Rename moves the epic's folder and the links to it; Complete skips its phases left and closes what waits on you; Delete deletes its folder, which the epic repo's history keeps. A done epic's menu has no Resume or Complete.</>
			<item>A star click writes the shared <link target="src-epics-favorites-json5" link="/epics/favorites.json5"><text code>epics/favorites.json5</></>, through <text code>POST /api/epics/favorite</>.</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-10-19 against branch <ui-text code>epic-engine</> (P3).</>
		</>
	</>
